  "interpretation": "The new mapper closes C10's real ICC-semantic luminance-domain gap without hard component clipping: it leaves every in-gamut float32 sample bit-exact, compresses only OOG OKLab lightness, and analytically scales chroma along the original (a,b) direction into the RGB16 interior. It is strongly hue-preserving and passes the existing style-safety envelope. It is not uniformly superior to local-MINDE: its median OOG OKLab mapping distance is 4.01x larger, while its median hue error is dramatically smaller. Treat the result as a non-dominated engineering trade-off that requires fresh profile/content confirmation, not as perceptual optimality.",
